  "final_message": "The book library is built, but I couldn't build the Docker image here because Docker isn't available, so the image and the frontend in a browser are untested.\n\nWhat I did check:\n- **Backend:** I exercised it in Flask's test client against a temporary database. That covered registration (including a duplicate username in a different case), login and bearer-token auth, and creating, listing with search, updating and deleting books. It also covered one review per user per book and the average rating.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` both pass.\n\nThe backend is `backend/app.py`. The frontend is React with Tailwind in `frontend/src/`. The database is `data/library.db`.\n\nValidation and behaviour I chose where the spec was silent:\n- **Duplicate username:** registering one that's taken answers 409. Usernames are case-insensitive.\n- **Book fields:** title and author are required (up to 200 characters), `year` must be 1\u20139999, and `isbn` is free text up to 32 characters.\n- **Review fields:** rating is a whole number from 1 to 5.\n- **Second review of a book:** answers 409.\n- **Passwords:** any non-empty password is accepted, with no minimum length.\n- **Tokens:** they last 30 days and are stored hashed.\n- **Validation errors:** these answer 400 with `{\"error\", \"errors\": {field: message}}`, and the forms show the per-field messages.\n\nI also added `.gitignore` and `frontend/tsconfig.json`.",
